      "message": "Should it be a map instead ? Like this (pseudo code):\n\n```\nprivate static final HashMap\u003cStrings, Consumer\u003cDevice\u003e\u003e atMap \u003d Map.ofEntries(\n  entry(BluetoothHeadset.VENDOR_SPECIFIC_HEADSET_EVENT_CGMI, processAtCgmi),\n  entry(BluetoothHeadset.VENDOR_SPECIFIC_HEADSET_EVENT_CGMM, processAtCgmm),\n  entry(BluetoothHeadset.VENDOR_SPECIFIC_HEADSET_EVENT_CGMR, processAtCgmr),\n  entry(BluetoothHeadset.VENDOR_SPECIFIC_HEADSET_EVENT_CGSN, processAtCgsn),\n  );\n\nConsumer\u003cDevice\u003e atConsumer \u003d atMap.get(atString);\nif (atConsumer !\u003d null) {\n  atConsumer.apply(device);\n  mNativeInterface.atResponseCode(device, HeadsetHalConstants.AT_RESPONSE_OK, 0);\n  return;\n}\n```\nadvantage:\n* one definition of atstring and it\u0027s consumer\n* no multiple ifs\n* no code execution in 2 places (one in the switch and one in the `if !miss`\n* compact code",
